Once upon a time, Paul <capelink99@hotmail.com> said:
>My problem is that what ever I seem to connect to it it doesn't see any
>devices - either on the Alpha or my PC. Am I just used to more modern cards
>??.. I don't know, but I thought most cards put themselves in Single-Ended
>mode if SE devices were fitted. Perhaps this is the problem, but when I
>connected up a modern U160 LVD drive it didn't see that either. I know there
>are Alpha SRM switches such as pkX0_soft_term but am I wasting my time in
>trying to fit a SE device to this card ?

There are three kinds of SCSI (well okay, there are more, but these are
what you are thinking about):

- single ended
- differential (now sometimes called high-voltage differential)
- LVD or low-voltage differential

Most (all?) LVD devices can fall back to single ended, but older devices
either talk differential or they talk single-ended - there is no fall
back or compatibility.

>Can these switches make the card see SE devices ?

Not as far as I know.

>Any ideas appreciated before it goes in the bin :-)

