The EEI (Extended Error Information) is being generated by your tape drive(s).  It 
is typically from a "soft" error or simple because the tape drive is reposition 
the tape.

It won't go away, and it is typically not a problem, so just ignore it.

(If you are using Legato Networker, it will cause the drive to generate this type 
of error on all reboots.)


