> to be able to allow someone to log directly into root.  This has to do 
> with X11 tunneling.
> 
> I've looked at /etc/securettys and was able to allow root access from 
> anywhere by putting in 'ptys' in the file.  That obviously is not what I 
> want.  I've looked at /etc/auth/system/ttys & /etc/auth/system/devassign 
> but can't figure out what to put in there.  Any ideas or help appreciated.
> 
> Thanks,
> Vic


FYI: Co-worker figured it out.  It seems that the root /.Xauthority file 
is not getting updated with the users cookie when they su to root.  To 
fix this we have to do this from root:

# /usr/bin/X11/xauth -f /.Xauthority merge /<user home 
directory>/.Xauthority

Then the user can '# su' to root (don't include '-') and run the X11 
application.

Vic




